WEBVTT

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.810
I like this world.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.390
I was a little confused 
when I first came here.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.100
But unlike my world, where we always

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.380
struggled over who would 
take power in the family,

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.090
this place suits me much better.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.960
So I want to live in a 
peaceful world forever.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.650
That's what I truly want.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.300
A haunted house?

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.590
Yes.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.870
There's a house that's 
supposed to have ghosts.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.630
Want to go and check it out over our three day weekend, Yoshiaki?

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.310
Sure, we can hang out over the weekend,

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:45.230
but why a haunted house?

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.390
<i>And no! No! No! No! No!</i>

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.010
<i>I'm scared of ghosts!</i>

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.190
Yoshiaki-chan,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.820
do you not like ghosts?

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.820
It's not that I don't like them...

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.190
But why me?

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:03.220
You were called the
Annihilate Princess, right?

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.120
Which means you're strong, right?

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
That was in my old world.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.410
And I've never fought a ghost.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.690
Murata-san will be joining 
us, too, so it's fine.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.970
<i>I know it's rude to say,</i>

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.560
<i>but she scares me just as much!</i>

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.490
Murata-san isn't coming, is she?

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:10.460
Not sure.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.170
Then maybe we shouldn't go.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.380
I mean, that occult 
stuff is her business.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.400
If she's not with us, we can't do it.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.250
There's still five minutes until 
the specified meeting time.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.890
We just got here a little early.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.330
Oh, yeah.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.520
And you were here a 
half hour early, Yoshiaki.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.390
You must've been really looking forward to this.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.530
Really?

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.920
<i>That's because I got scared of being 
home alone with all that ghost talk.</i>

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.590
Scary, huh?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.240
Yeah? You, too, Yumi-chan?

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.970
Date Masamune-san?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.740
Wanted

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.740
Violation of the Firearms Control Law 
Attempted Murder 
Drug Smuggling 
Dine and Dash

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.740
<b>Date Masamune</b>

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.740
Apparently, she's a dangerous 
criminal on the run.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.470
There used to be a rumor that she was

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:51.380
hiding around here, not too long ago.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.050
They say she not only sold drugs,

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:56.710
but she also put a lot of her fellow 
gang members in the hospital.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.250
She's really scary.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.180
Do you know her, Yoshiaki-chan?

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.630
Oh, Masamune, yeah?

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:10.850
She was famous back home, so yeah.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:15.810
My, my.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.430
You're still wetting 
the bed at your age?

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.400
Auntie.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.820
Don't call me Auntie!

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.050
It's this house's fault 
for being so creepy!

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.440
There might be ghosts around!

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.570
Oh, dear.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:29.930
You wish to be the next 
head of the family,

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.960
and yet you would insult the 
noble house of the Date?

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.250
Sure I will!

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.700
And the first thing I'm gonna do

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.310
when I'm head of the family 
is rebuild this haunted house.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:45.590
She was rude, gruff and really mean.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:50.660
But you didn't dislike her, did you?

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.980
Not especially.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.410
She was nice from time to time.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.570
Shall we... get going?!

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.780
Okay, everybody, let's go!

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.930
This is nice.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:38.190
This is how we want it.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:41.600
Doesn't look a thing 
like a haunted house!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.110
The windows are all boarded up.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.250
So you can't see what's 
going on from the outside.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.700
Or from the inside.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.080
Is it okay to go in without permission?

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.290
You don't have to worry about that.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:01.200
My aunt recently bought the property.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.580
Really?

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:08.300
Yes. She wants us to see if there 
are actually any ghosts here.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.660
Your aunt?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.850
Are you and your aunt close, Mao-chan?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:13.750
Yes.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:16.840
Are you not, Yoshiaki-chan?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.350
In my case, she was a rival.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:23.300
And in my case, I'm the aunt.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.910
It's dark.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.620
Well, the power's off.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.150
There should be a generator.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:36.120
It's in the basement.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.490
I'll go.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.180
I'll go with you.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:42.360
You gonna be okay, Mao-chan?

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:42.880
Huh?

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:47.970
Wouldn't we be more in danger 
since we don't have a light?

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:49.410
Yeah.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.490
They're not back yet.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:00.920
They shouldn't be long.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:03.940
How long have you been there?!

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.200
I'm back.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.320
Welcome back.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.070
There was a strange, 
powerful energy in the basement.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:15.660
So if we know that, then we don't 
need to do anything else.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.020
What do you mean?

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.430
We have to find out what it is.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.460
Murata-san, was it an evil energy?

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.960
I couldn't say.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.690
Then we need to find out.

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.720
Okay, let's go.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.720
Is this it?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.600
Yes, I believe so.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.650
An underground chapel?

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:44.560
Looks ghostly!

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.920
What? It's not opening!

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.750
It's not even moving.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.080
That's strange.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.550
I don't see a lock on the door.

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:58.990
Are they making sure it
only opens from the inside?

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.000
Do you mean the ghosts 
are making it that way?

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.580
But if it's only from the inside,

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.770
that means they're locking themselves in.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:06.750
Which means...

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:10.650
They might not be bad ghosts.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.300
Either way, it doesn't open.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.510
So why don't we look at it later?

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.760
But if we're going to tell her aunt 
what's going on, we need to find out.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:22.020
If we look elsewhere, we might 
figure out how to open it.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.480
Yes, that seems like our best option.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.020
I guess we don't need to hurry.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.280
We're staying here tonight?

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.090
Yes. That was the original plan.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.280
And the last train home's already left.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.670
You're right.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.620
<i>Glance.</i>

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.060
Can I choose my own room?

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:50.380
Sure.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.390
Your own room?

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.970
You mean we're all sleeping alone?

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.260
Is that a problem?

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.670
What's the matter, Yoshiaki?

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:58.860
Are you scared?

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.420
I'm not scared.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:03.380
But it's kinda lonely that way.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:05.560
Don't you think so, Mao-chan?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.360
Mao-chan, sleep in a room with me, okay?

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.690
I kick in my sleep and 
it's embarrassing.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:16.030
I see.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.660
All right, then.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.720
There sure are a lot of rooms here!

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.800
We could stay in a different 
room every day.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:28.380
Oh yeah, we're here for
three days and two nights...

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.370
How about this room?

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:37.180
Looks like a mummy storage room.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.630
Jeez.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:39.910
Can't sleep here.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.190
Can't get a good night's 
sleep next to a mummy.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.130
I can.

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:47.900
<i>That's not the problem.</i>

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:51.150
<i>There's something wrong with this place.</i>

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:55.430
<i>I have to go to the bathroom.</i>

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:57.950
I guess the third room we 
saw was probably the best.

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:00.300
The third?

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.690
It looked like a bedroom, right?

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.160
Yoshiaki-chan, do you not feel well?

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.040
No...

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:08.920
Well...

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.750
Oh, you have to go to the bathroom.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:12.590
Yeah.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.500
The bathroom...

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:17.760
The bathroom is right 
back the way we came.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.490
Don't scare me.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.360
Come to think of it, 
I did see one.

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:22.720
Hurry up and go.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.300
Alone?

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.170
Anybody else need to go?

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.020
Then, maybe I'll just hold it.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:36.280
We may come across another.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.410
<i>We haven't!</i>

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.680
<i>I can't hold it anymore.</i>

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.200
Okay, then here's fine.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.440
Mao-chan, I can't possibly do it here.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:51.250
Oh, the room.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.180
You're the only one left, Yoshiaki.

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:55.880
I'll take this room.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:56.890
Really?

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.130
Yeah, it's right next to Mao-chan.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.010
You really sure?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:03.810
It was too much for me.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:18.270
Perhaps I'll take another room.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:20.950
I think that would be best.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:34.770
It's such a big mansion,

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.010
but this is the only bathroom on the first floor.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.570
Yeah, seems so.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.840
There may be others if we look.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.670
Then we can go exploring tomorrow.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:46.600
<i>The others aren't scared at all,</i>

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.960
<i>even though there's something 
in the basement.</i>

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.020
Let's eat.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.020
This is great.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.030
You're a good cook, Mao.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.440
It's just a hobby.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.140
A hobby?

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:03.500
It's really good.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.890
Thank you.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.990
I'm glad to hear that from you.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.920
But it's really good.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.750
What's this, an earthquake?

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:13.830
<i>It's not.</i>

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:16.850
<i>The chandelier isn't moving.</i>

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:17.840
<i>Is this...</i>

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:20.480
<i>a poltergeist?!</i>

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:26.260
Murata-san, what are you doing?!

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:30.490
During an earthquake, you're 
supposed to get under a table,

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:32.270
didn't you know that?

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:34.350
An earthquake?

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.010
Yes. It's stopped now, though.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:41.030
Good night, then.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.030
Good night.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:49.000
That's Murata-san again, isn't it?

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.550
I can't take this place anymore!

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:07.290
You're worrying too much.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.530
It didn't turn out to 
be anything, right?

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.310
Sure, but...

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:16.360
Murata-san said the ghost in the 
basement isn't evil, right?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.300
That's true, but...

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.570
It's fine.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:25.470
Even if it's a nasty ghost, 
leave it to Murata-san.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:31.270
Yumi-chan?

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:35.890
What is this?!

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:39.290
It's not an evil ghost, <i>right</i>?

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:41.630
That's right. I'm pretty sure.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:44.550
But something's off about this place!

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:48.050
I'll take a look, then.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:52.930
I can see it.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:02.630
What's wrong?

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.280
It wasn't just one.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:09.080
It wasn't just one!

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:09.080
Murata-san!

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:11.910
Murata-san...

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.000
Is she okay?

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.010
She'll come back.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:17.890
There's nowhere else for her to go.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:21.190
Yumi-chan, aren't you bothered about
what happened in the shower?

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.920
I'm pretty sure it was just rusty pipes.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.720
Seriously?

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:27.930
What do you think, Mao-chan?

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:33.430
Either way, we should wait 
for Murata-san to come back.

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:41.280
<i>How far did she run?</i>

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:45.860
What if I have to go to the 
bathroom again while I'm waiting?

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.950
The bathroom's that way, isn't it?

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.210
Yumi-chan?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.690
Yoshiaki...

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:05.590
Sorry!

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.840
What was I...

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.820
Something may have been possessing you.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.220
Possessing me?

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:17.430
Oh. I'll go back to bed...

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:21.550
Yumi-chan?

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:24.800
Yumi-chan!

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.360
Mao-chan!

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.060
Yumi-chan needs help!

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:35.260
Mao-chan?

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:37.870
Yumi-chan!

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.170
That's Yumi-chan's...

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:48.540
It's my fault, for saying that we should

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:50.900
check out the underground chapel later...

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:55.220
If we had figured it out first, 
this wouldn't have happened.

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.560
To be honest, I'm scared.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:02.980
I don't like being alone, 
and I want to run away.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:03.730
But...

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:08.110
I'm the only one who can save them now.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:09.530
I'll do it!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.200
Come out,

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.580
you evil ghost that's hiding here!

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:32.500
<i>She's going to kill me!</i>

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:41.820
Masamune?

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.100
Masamune?

00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:56.530
You're awake.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:59.540
Is that you, Auntie?

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:02.300
I told you not to call me that.

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:03.450
That attitude...

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:06.120
It's definitely you, Auntie.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.540
Forget it.

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:10.230
So, what were you thinking by

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:12.370
trying to kill somebody?

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.050
I was trying to knock out a pursuer.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:17.510
You were holding it the wrong way.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:19.700
Don't swing a katana around

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.560
when you're about to pass out.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.780
So you're going to clam up 
when you realize I'm right?

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:29.560
You always treat me like a kid, too.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.470
Which of us is the kid?

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:35.900
You're right, Auntie.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:38.470
I told you to stop calling me that!

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:40.820
And why are you agreeing?

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.410
That's not like you.

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.650
I've learned that...

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:48.420
I'm naïve.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.710
Did you learn how good 
Kojuuro-san is for you?

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.350
Very much so.

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:55.300
I see.

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:02.410
You could at least say thanks 
before you start eating.

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:04.390
Thanks.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.180
You must've been really hungry.

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:10.850
Hey, Masamune.

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:13.900
Do you want me to talk 
to Yoshiteru-chan?

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.160
By Yoshiteru, do you mean 
Ashikaga Yoshiteru?

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.270
Yes, that's right.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.670
You got part of your name 
from hers, didn't you?

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:28.960
Yes. Yoshiaki is written as Yoshiteru
without part of the last kanji.

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:32.670
She'll help you.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:35.340
If you want to stay in this world,

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:38.120
you shouldn't commit any more crimes.

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:41.680
You're planning to stay in 
this world, aren't you?

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:44.110
Yes, why?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:48.190
Then please stay away from me.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.270
Why do you say that?

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:55.610
My destruction of the Midori 
gang is a crime in this world.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.360
But, you can ask Yoshiteru-chan...

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.570
A crime is a crime, Auntie.

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:05.710
If I ask Yoshiteru-dono, 
the authorities may stop chasing me,

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.360
but my crime won't disappear.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:13.750
And what will people think of 
you when you side with me...

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.620
If you're going to live 
here in this world,

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:22.760
you shouldn't lose your 
stature for my sake, Auntie.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.260
But I can't just leave you!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.210
Now that we've met like this...

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:29.370
We never met.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.620
All that's here is a single black cat.

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:33.150
Tell them that.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:34.760
But, Masamune...

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.280
This time I held the blade 
the right way, Auntie.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.250
Masamune...

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:36.900
Yoshiaki, I just heard this 
loud noise. What's up?

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.290
Nothing, really.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:40.340
Wait, you're okay?

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:41.770
Yeah, I guess.

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:43.620
Just a light concussion?

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:45.320
I'm relatively unhurt.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:49.640
Honestly, it hurts most 
where you slapped me.

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:50.350
I see.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:54.220
You went back to your room after 
I went to find Mao-chan, right?

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:55.690
Where's Mao-chan?

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:59.210
Isn't she in your room?

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:14.940
Did you see?

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.830
No, I just got here.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.210
Did you find something?

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:22.990
Yeah.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:26.060
I found a cat in the chapel.

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:28.220
But it didn't want 
anything to do with me.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:30.760
I gave it some food,

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.360
but when it had eaten its fill, it left.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.400
And then... And then...

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:43.070
Get some sleep.

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:47.820
This time, I'll watch you while you sleep.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:52.090
That's kind of embarrassing.

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:58.000
Hey, if you're still sleepy...

00:21:58.510 --> 00:21:59.840
want to sleep in the same bed?

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:03.150
Yeah.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:05.670
I don't have anything to be
embarrassed about anymore.

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:49.740
Next time it's the blade adept, 
Ashikaga Yoshiteru-sama!

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:53.460
Next time on Sengoku 
Collection: "Blade Adept!"

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:56.730
Actually, I got my name 
from Yoshiteru-chan!

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:59.840
Wait, did I already say that?
